   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# CPEC detection: RetinaNet training v2\nSame model as the original notebook, with these changes:\n1. **Augmentation that actually works for RetinaNet.** Flips and 90\u00b0 rotations move the box targets with the image, and per-channel colour jitter simulates stain variation. The original generator only applied contrast, and per-tile normalization cancelled most of it.\n2. **Optional new anchors.** Re-encodes the pickled targets for more anchor scales and ratios.\n3. **Learning-rate schedule.** Reduces the learning rate when validation loss plateaus.\n4. **Checkpoint chosen by detection F1**, not by eye.\n\nRun `CPEC detection evaluation.ipynb` on the old model first so you have a baseline to compare against."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "import pickle, glob\nimport numpy as np, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom tensorflow import keras\nfrom tensorflow.keras import Input\nfrom jarvis.train.box import BoundingBox\nimport biondi\nimport cpec_tools as ct",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "training_dataset_dir = ''\nvalidation_dataset_dir = ''\nwith open(training_dataset_dir, 'rb') as f: x = pickle.load(f)\nwith open(validation_dataset_dir, 'rb') as f: v = pickle.load(f)\n\nbb_orig = BoundingBox(image_shape=(256, 256), classes=1, c=[3], anchor_shapes=[16],\n                      anchor_scales=[1], anchor_ratios=[1], iou_upper=0.5, iou_lower=0.2)",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## Anchors\nLeave `CHANGE_ANCHORS = False` to keep the original anchors. Set it to `True` only if the box-size report in the evaluation notebook shows many cells that 16 px square anchors can't match.\n\nChange one thing at a time (augmentation first, then anchors) so you can tell what helped."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "CHANGE_ANCHORS = False\n\nif CHANGE_ANCHORS:\n    scales, ratios = [0.8, 1, 1.26, 1.6], [1]      # keep ratios=[1] to allow 90-degree rotation augmentation\n    bb = BoundingBox(image_shape=(256, 256), classes=1, c=[3], anchor_shapes=[16],\n                     anchor_scales=scales, anchor_ratios=ratios, iou_upper=0.5, iou_lower=0.3)\n    x = ct.reencode_targets(x, bb_orig, bb)\n    v = ct.reencode_targets(v, bb_orig, bb)\n    A = len(scales) * len(ratios)\nelse:\n    bb, A = bb_orig, 1",
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
